# Copy to .env and adjust. .env is gitignored — real values never get committed.

# VNC password. Required — if unset, wayvnc runs with NO authentication,
# which is fine for a quick local test but not for anything reachable off localhost.
VNC_PASSWORD=changeme

# Host port to publish the VNC server on.
VNC_PORT=5900

# --- Remote MCP bridge (optional, see SETUP.md's "Studio MCP over the network") ---
# Not needed unless you want a remote MCP client (e.g. Claude Code elsewhere) to reach
# Roblox Studio's built-in MCP server through this container. entrypoint.sh
# auto-starts the bridge whenever MCP_TOKEN is non-empty — leave it commented out
# (unset) to skip the bridge entirely, same as leaving VNC_PASSWORD unset skips VNC auth.

# Host port to publish the MCP bridge (Caddy, bearer-token gated) on.
MCP_PORT=8787

# Bearer token remote MCP clients must send. Generate with: openssl rand -hex 32
# Treat this like a credential — the MCP tools it gates can execute arbitrary Luau code
# inside Roblox Studio (see research/roblox-mcp.md §5.4). Deliberately left commented
# out (not a "changeme" placeholder like VNC_PASSWORD above) — an uncommented weak
# default here would silently auto-start the bridge with a guessable token.
#MCP_TOKEN=

# Optional override for the stdio command that launches Studio's built-in MCP server
# process. Defaults to /usr/local/bin/studio-mcp-stdio.sh (bakes in the resolved,
# tested-working command — see that script's own header comment) — leave unset unless
# you have a specific reason to point at something else.
#STUDIO_MCP_STDIO_CMD=
